{%- comment -%}
  The mark next to a promise. One shape, used by every slot, so the row cannot
  drift into three different icons — and so a change of mind about the shape is
  one edit rather than three.

  It is inline SVG rather than an image because it is 120 bytes, needs no
  request, takes its colour from the text beside it, and stays sharp on the
  wall's texture at any density. `aria-hidden` because the words next to it
  already say what it means; a screen reader announcing "circular arrow" ahead
  of "14-day exchange" is noise.
{%- endcomment -%}
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <path d="M20 12a8 8 0 1 1-2.34-5.66"/>
  <path d="M20 4v4.5h-4.5"/>
</svg>
